  "primer": {
    "$comment": "One Dark palette for gen-primer-theme. Source: https://github.com/joshdick/onedark.vim autoload/onedark.vim (MIT) — black/bg #282c34, cursor_grey #2c323c, special_grey #3b4048, visual/menu_grey #3e4452, gutter_fg_grey #4b5263, comment_grey #5c6370, white/fg #abb2bf, red #e06c75, dark_red #be5046, green #98c379, yellow #e5c07b, dark_yellow #d19a66, blue #61afef, purple #c678dd, cyan #56b6c2. Base: @primer/primitives dark. Canvas bg, raised cursor_grey, borders visual_grey / gutter grey, text fg; comment_grey is 2.3:1 on bg, so muted is a derived #9299a7 (between comment and fg) and comment_grey is disabled. Accent + primary button + link blue (dark text), success green, danger red (text lightened to #da7880, red is 4.4:1; dark_red for emphasis bgs), attention yellow, severe dark_yellow, done + sponsors purple. Nothing darker than bg, so inset/shadow #1b1e24 is derived (the Atom One Dark sidebar shade).",
